      "message": "IIRC, the test: \n1. Clear `interrupt_counter`.\n2. Set rtc alram to 1 second and wait for the timeout.\n3. When the timeout happens, the driver invokes an interrupt handler/ callback to set `interrupt_counter`.\n4. Check if `interrupt_counter` is 1.   \n\nIn the test code, you only implemented step 1, 2 and miss the step 3 because the interrupt callback is [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/rtc.c;l\u003d29) and it doesn\u0027t set `interrupt_counter`\nThis is why the test cannot pass.\nIMO, overriding the callback to set `interrupt_counter` should fix the code to pass the test.",
